只输出严格JSON，恰好包含id（metadata.id原样）、summary_zh（15到140个Unicode字符，通常40到100字）、category（枚举）、tags（2到5个不重复关键词，每个最多30字符）、confidence（0到1，仅自评）、insufficient_evidence（布尔）、evidence（1到3个对象，每个恰好包含paragraph_id、fact）、limitations（0到5个字符串）。只选择输入中长度20至120字符的完整片段编号；fact是该片段支持的中文事实转述。不要输出quote，不要自行抄写、拼接、删改或补造引用。程序会按编号附上原文。一个编号只用一次；最多3条证据。不得增加字段。
摘要和limitations保留会改变功能意义的前提、平台例外和限制：设密码后才认证、页面保持打开才提醒、依赖外部组件、估算不等于保证。只写已实现功能，不将规划当完成。证据不足就标记，不编造。
图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Playwright/CDP web-fetch provider for DeepSeek Harness: renders pages in a real browser, denoises them (Readability + DOMPurify), and returns markdown.","id":"gh:1341712226","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-web-fetch-playwright","slug":"chendefine/dsh-web-fetch-playwright","topics":["cordis","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-bundle","dsh-plugin","fetch-provider","markdown","playwright","web-fetch"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Playwright/CDP web-fetch provider for DeepSeek Harness: renders pages in a real browser, denoises th"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"em (Readability + DOMPurify), and returns markdown."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-web-fetch-playwright"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"中文 · npm · GitHub"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"A DeepSeek Harness (DSH) plugin that gives the built-in `web_fetch` tool a **Playwright/CDP backend*"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"*: pages are rendered in a real browser, denoised with **Readability + DOMPurify + Turndown + GFM**,"},{"id":"p4s3","text":" and returned as Markdown."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"## Features"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"- **Real browser rendering** — loads the page the way a user sees it, so client-side rendered (SPA) "},{"id":"p6s2","text":"content is captured, not just the raw HTML.\n- **Denoise pipeline** — Mozilla Readability extracts th"},{"id":"p6s3","text":"e article, DOMPurify removes layout/noise tags (nav, sidebar, footer, ads, forms), and Turndown with"},{"id":"p6s4","text":" the GFM plugin converts to Markdown with the same style options as the shipped `tool-web` renderer."},{"id":"p6s5","text":" Inline `data:` images (build tools like Docusaurus embed screenshots as base64) are elided to size "},{"id":"p6s6","text":"placeholders such as `!alt` so they cannot flood the body. On list-shaped pages (portals, catalogs) "},{"id":"p6s7","text":"where the content *is* the links, Readability's link-density scoring picks a noise fragment — a cove"},{"id":"p6s8","text":"rage gate therefore distrusts an extraction under 250 characters or covering under 10% of the page's"},{"id":"p6s9","text":" visible text (measured on the 163.com homepage: 96 characters of footer licensing won while 320 hea"},{"id":"p6s10","text":"dlines scored near zero), and the pipeline falls back to the sanitized whole document, which on such"},{"id":"p6s11","text":" pages keeps effectively all list content.\n- **Two backends** — launch a local Playwright browser, o"},{"id":"p6s12","text":"r drive an already-running browser over its DevTools Protocol (CDP) endpoint.\n- **Browser resolution"},{"id":"p6s13","text":"** — a configured path, a `playwright` CLI on `$PATH`, or the bundled `playwright-core`; CDP needs n"},{"id":"p6s14","text":"o local browser at all.\n- **Shared profile or reusable isolation (CDP)** — each fetch opens and clos"},{"id":"p6s15","text":"es its own tab; session isolation uses a dedicated CDP connection per DSH session, while global/prof"},{"id":"p6s16","text":"ile modes share one connection. By default it uses the browser's existing default context and logins"},{"id":"p6s17","text":" (`connectOverCDP` → `browser.contexts()[0]`, like CLI CDP attach with isolation disabled, not `play"},{"id":"p6s18","text":"wright-cli open`). Session isolation creates an in-memory context on demand and shares it only while"},{"id":"p6s19","text":" same-session fetches or other tabs keep it in use; global isolation retains one fixed isolated cont"},{"id":"p6s20","text":"ext across all sessions within the same plugin instance. Local launches still close their browser pe"},{"id":"p6s21","text":"ssions within the same plugin instance. Local launches still close their browser per fetch.\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## How it works"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"| Half | Location | Responsibility |"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"| Host (server) | `src/` | Registers the fetch provider (id `playwright`) into `ctx.web`; `cordis.pa"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"tch.yml` pins the web seam's `fetchProvider` to it and enables the `web_fetch` tool with a 60s budge"},{"id":"p9s3","text":"t. |\n| Browser (client) | `src/client/` | Registers the *Playwright web fetch* configuration form on"},{"id":"p9s4","text":" the Plugins page's `plugins.bundle.config` / `plugins.row.config` seats, which stages edits and wri"},{"id":"p9s5","text":"tes them through the shared settings form service. |"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"**Non-2xx statuses are results, not errors** — the web seam's contract (`@deepseek-ai/dsh-web`): a f"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"etched 404/418/500 comes back with its status code, exactly what `dsh-web-fetch-http` does. Chromium"},{"id":"p11s3","text":" complicates this for *status-only* responses — an error status with an empty body (httpbin's `/stat"},{"id":"p11s4","text":"us/404`) fails the whole navigation with `net::ERR_HTTP_RESPONSE_CODE_FAILURE`, and a 204/205 is abo"},{"id":"p11s5","text":"rted (`net::ERR_ABORTED`) because nothing is renderable. The provider therefore tracks the last main"},{"id":"p11s6","text":"-frame response on every fetch (that response arrives before Chromium fails the navigation) and reco"},{"id":"p11s7","text":"vers such failures into the status-bearing result, so `web_fetch` reports `Fetched … (HTTP 404)` ins"},{"id":"p11s8","text":"tead of a `WEB_PROVIDER_ERROR` throw. The same recovery covers *download* responses — a body served "},{"id":"p11s9","text":"with `Content-Disposition: attachment` (publish.twitter.com's oembed endpoint, the URL agents use to"},{"id":"p11s10","text":" read a tweet, serves its JSON exactly that way) never commits a document: `goto` rejects with `Down"},{"id":"p11s11","text":"load is starting` and the body is gone from the network stack, so the provider refetches it through "},{"id":"p11s12","text":"the page's API request context and returns the decodable content; undecodable downloads (a PDF, a ZI"},{"id":"p11s13","text":"e's API request context and returns the decodable content; undecodable downloads (a PDF, a ZI [长行截断]"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"## Requirements"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"- DSH web profile (`dsh web`), Node.js ≥ 20.\n- For the **local** backend: a Playwright installation "},{"id":"p14s2","text":"with Chromium, a Chromium-family browser binary, or `playwright-core` with a browser in the default "},{"id":"p14s3","text":"cache.\n- For the **CDP** backend: any browser already running with `--remote-debugging-port` (e.g. `"},{"id":"p14s4","text":"chromium --headless --remote-debugging-port=9222`)."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"## Installation"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"From the npm registry (prebuilt — no build permission needed):"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"From a GitHub repository (source — pnpm runs the `prepare` build; allowlist the package in `profiles"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"/web/pnpm-workspace.yaml` if pnpm blocks the build script):"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"Or through the DSH plugin marketplace (设置 → DSH插件市场) — the repo carries the `dsh-plugin` topic and i"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"s indexed automatically."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"After a bundle plugin is added to the profile layer stack, **restart `dsh web`** for it to load; uni"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"nstall with `dsh plugin --profile web remove dsh-web-fetch-playwright` and restart again."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"## Configuration"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"The Plugins page (侧边栏 → 插件) opens the form one click from the list: the *dsh-web-fetch-playwright* c"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"ard lands on the package page with the full form between its description and its rows, and the row's"},{"id":"p23s3","text":" own configure control opens the same form under the plugin's title. It edits the `web-fetch-playwri"},{"id":"p23s4","text":"ght` settings section — derived from the plugin entry's `Config` schema — live:"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"## Security"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"Same stance as the built-in HTTP provider: **no SSRF / private-network protection is implemented** —"},{"id":"p26s2","text":" anything the browser can reach, this provider can fetch. The CDP endpoint is configured from the se"},{"id":"p26s3","text":"ttings page with no loopback restriction, so only expose the settings page to trusted environments. "},{"id":"p26s4","text":"Fetched pages are rendered locally; no data is sent anywhere beyond the target page itself — but not"},{"id":"p26s5","text":"e that in profile mode the requests (and any state changes a malicious page tricks the agent into) c"},{"id":"p26s6","text":"arry the remote browser's logged-in sessions (see the risk notes above)."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
